Done. Two files changed:

**`src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Finds notes whose `tags` vector contains the exact tag string (not substring), preserving input order.

**`src/main.rs`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into `list`:
- Parses `--tag` from args using `windows(2)` (finds the `--tag` token, reads the next arg as the tag value).
- When present, calls `filter_by_tag` before printing.
- When absent, behaves as before (prints all notes).

